\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The foe behind, the deep before,
\par Our hosts have dared and passed the sea;
\par And Pharaoh's warriors strew the shore,
\par And Israel's ransomed tribes are free.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Lift up, lift up your voices now!
\par The whole wide world rejoices now!
\par The Lord hath triumphed gloriously!
\par The Lord shall reign victoriously!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Happy morrow, Turning sorrow
\par Into peace and mirth!
\par Bondage ending, Love descending
\par O'er the earth!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Seals assuring, Guards securing,
\par Watch His earthly prison:
\par Seals are shattered; Guards are scattered;
\par Christ hath risen!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. No longer must the mourners weep,
\par Nor call departed Christians dead;
\par For death is hallowed into sleep,
\par And every grave becomes a bed.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Now once more
\par Eden's door
\par Open stands to mortal eyes;
\par For Christ hath risen, and man shall rise!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Now at last, 
\par Old things past,
\par Hope, and joy, and peace begin;
\par For Christ hath won, and man shall win!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. It is not exile, rest on high;
\par It is not sadness, peace from strife;
\par To fall asleep is not to die;
\par To dwell with Christ is better life.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 9. Where our banner leads us,
\par We may safely go;
\par Where our Chief precedes us,
\par We may face the foe.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 10\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 10. His right arm is o'er us,
\par He our Guide will be:
\par Christ hath gone before us;
\par Christians, follow ye!
\par \cf1\ul\b\f1 
\par \f2 
\par }

